  "reasoning_content": "We need answer user: \"Write a detailed tutorial on implementing a bounded LRU cache in Python using collections.OrderedDict. Include a complete class, explain get and put behavior, discuss edge cases, and include tests. Continue with a worked example and complexity analysis. Be precise and use meaningful prose and code.\"\n\nNeed produce final tutorial. Must include complete class, explain get/put, edge cases, tests, worked example, complexity analysis. Need maybe mention OrderedDict move_to_end. Bounded LRU cache. Could implement LeetCode-like LRUCache with capacity, get, put, maybe clear? Need precise. Edge cases: capacity zero/negative? key equality/hashability, mutable values? missing key, update existing key, evict LRU, thread safety? OrderedDict in CPython, but not thread-safe without lock. Need tests. Worked example step-by-step. Complexity O(1) get/put amortized? OrderedDict O(1) average. Python hash O(1) average. Need maybe code runnable.\n\nLet's craft robust class. Use OrderedDict. Behavior:\n- __init__(capacity: int): if capacity < 1 raise ValueError.\n- get(key, default=None): if key not in cache return default; move_to_end(key) to mark most recent; return cache[key].\n- put(key, value): if key in cache: update value and move_to_end; else if len >= capacity: popitem(last=False) evict least recently used; cache[key]=value.\nCould include __len__, __contains__, __getitem__, __setitem__, clear? The user says complete class, bounded LRU cache. Could include enough. If using OrderedDict directly: self._cache = OrderedDict(); capacity. For get, use try/except or key in. Using 'in' O(1). move_to_end after get/put.\n\nNeed discuss edge cases:\n- capacity <= 0: reject or allow no storage? Better raise ValueError. Alternative allow zero with no storage. We can state design choice.\n- duplicate key updates: should update and refresh recency.\n- non-string keys? Any hashable. Values any object. Mutable values: cache stores references; modifying after put doesn't trigger LRU update; not copy.\n- default on missing get.\n- Eviction: least recently used (oldest end) removed when full and inserting new key.\n- get updates recency; put updates recency whether existing or new.\n- OrderedDict behavior",
